# What's my local AI?

Detect your hardware right in your browser and find out which local models you can run locally with Ollama or LM Studio.
Nothing is uploaded.

## Pages

- [Home]({{ site.url }}/): Check the best model you can run on your own machine in the browser, with nothing uploaded
- [Models]({{ site.url }}/models/): Every model that fits, and the closest ones that do not
- [Cost]({{ site.url }}/cost/): Local cost compared with a frontier API and DeepSeek
- [Setups]({{ site.url }}/setups/): Four machines that clear 20 tok/s, what they run, and roughly what they cost
- [How it works]({{ site.url }}/how-it-works/): Detection, ranking, speed, cost, and data sources
- [Use cases]({{ site.url }}/use-cases/): What people do with local models
- [Credits]({{ site.url }}/credits/): Technologies and libraries used to build the What's my local AI website

## Documentation

- [LM Studio](https://lmstudio.ai): Local model runner supported by the tool and offered as a runner choice in the interface
- [Ollama](https://ollama.com): Local model runner supported by the tool and offered as a runner choice in the interface
- [MLX](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx): Apple's inference framework; both supported runners ship MLX engines on Apple Silicon

## Source

- [GitHub - clubmatto/vetrina](https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina): Open source monorepo containing the source of this site
- [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co): Model repository used to source local models and weights for the tool
